1hfx|n|A wedge, or block made to fit in any space which it is desired to fill, esp. something to steady a cask or other body, or prevent it from moving, by fitting into the space around or beneath it. ; A heavy casting of metal, usually fixed near the gunwale. It has two short horn-shaped arms curving inward, between which ropes or hawsers may pass for towing, mooring, etc. ; An encounter.	V:zmy,19,1~zmy,19,1	n:aiv4,63,9;eje,4,8~aiv4,63,9;eje,4,8	N:931m,81,6;3ifa,25,6;zid,23,5;zmy,19,1~931m,81,6;3ifa,25,6;zid,23,5;zmy,19,1
